Travel Dua'a

Allahu akbaru kabira — Allahu akbaru kabira — Allahu akbaru kabira;

Subhanalladhi sakhkhara lana hadha wa ma kunna lahu muqrinin;

Wa inna ila rabbina lamunqalibun;

Allahumma inna nas’aluka fi safarina hadha al-birra wat-taqwa;

Wa minal-‘amali ma tardha;

Allahumma hawwin ‘alayna safarana hadha;

Wa’twi ‘anna bu‘dah;

Allahumma anta as-sahibu fis-safar;

Wal-khalifatu fil-ahl;

Allahumma inni a‘udhu bika min wa‘tha’is-safar;

Wa kaabatil-manzar;

Wa suu’il-munqalabi fil-mali wal-ahl;

Ayyibun, ta’ibun, ‘abidun, lirabbina hamidun.

Resident's duaa for the traveler

Astawdi‘u Allaha dinak;

Wa amanatak;

Wa khawatima ‘amalik.

Master of forgiveness

Allahumma anta rabbi, la ilaha illa anta;

Khalaqtani wa ana ‘abduk;

Wa ana ‘ala ‘ahdika wa wa‘dika ma istata‘tu;

A‘udhu bika min sharri ma sana‘tu;

Abu’u laka bini‘matika ‘alayya;

Wa abu’u laka bidhanbi;

Faghfir li, fa innahu la yaghfirudh-dhunuba illa anta.

When wearing clothes

Alhamdu lillahil-ladhi kasani hadha ath-thawb;

Wa razaqanihi min ghayri hawlin minni wa la quwwah.

Wearing new clothes

Allahumma laka al-hamdu, anta kasawtaniyah;

As’aluka min khayrih wa khayri ma suni‘a lah;

Wa a‘udhu bika min sharrih wa sharri ma suni‘a lah.

Supplication for someone who wears new clothes

Tubli wa yukhlifullahu ta‘ala.

Ilbas jadidan;

Wa ‘ish hamidan;

Wa mut shahidan.

When riding (car or similar)

Bismillah, walhamdu lillah;

Subhanalladhi sakhkhara lana hadha wa ma kunna lahu muqrinin;

Wa inna ila rabbina lamunqalibun;

Alhamdu lillah, alhamdu lillah, alhamdu lillah;

Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar;

Subhanaka Allahumma inni zalamtu nafsi faghfir li;

Fa innahu la yaghfirudh-dhunuba illa ant.

Expiation of a gathering

Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdik;

Ashhadu an la ilaha illa anta;

Astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk.

When seeing someone afflicted (with illness or hardship), say:

Alhamdu lillahil-ladhi ‘afani mimma ibtalaka bih;

Wa faddalani ‘ala kathirin mimman khalaqa tafdila.

Duaa for someone who finds something difficult

Allahumma la sahl illa ma ja‘altahu sahlan;

Wa anta taj‘alu al-hazna idha shi’ta sahlan.

Duaa for distress

La ilaha illallahu al-‘azimu al-halim;

La ilaha illallahu rabbul-‘arshil-‘azim;

La ilaha illallahu rabbus-samawati wa rabbul-ardi wa rabbul-‘arshil-karim;

Allahumma rahmataka arju, fala takilni ila nafsi tarfata ‘ayn,

Wa aslih li sha’ni kullah, la ilaha illa anta;

La ilaha illa anta subhanaka inni kuntu minaz-zalimin;

Allahu Allahu rabbi, la ushriku bihi shay’an.

Duaa for worry and sadness

Allahumma inni ‘abduka, ibnu ‘abdik, ibnu amatika;

Nasiati biyadik, madin fiyya hukmuk, ‘adlun fiyya qada’uk;

As’aluka bikulli ismin huwa lak, sammaita bihi nafsak;

Aw anzaltahu fi kitabik, aw ‘allamtahu ahadan min khalqik;

Aw ista’tharta bihi fi ‘ilmil-ghaybi ‘indak;

An taj‘alal-Qur’ana rabi‘a qalbi, wa nura sadri;

Wa jala’a huzni, wa dhahaba hammi.

Allahumma inni a‘udhu bika minal-hammi wal-hazan;

Wal-‘ajzi wal-kasal;

Wal-bukhli wal-jubn;

Wa dal‘id-dayni wa ghalabatir-rijal.

If you sin: say & do

Ma min ‘abdin yudhnibu dhanban;

Fayuhsinu at-tuhur;

Thumma yaqumu fayusalli rak‘atayn;

Thumma yastaghfirullah;

Illa ghafarallahu lah.

Before ablution:

Bismillah.

After ablution:

Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah wahdahu la sharika lah;

Wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan ‘abduhu wa rasuluh;

Allahumma aj‘alni minat-tawwabin;

Waj‘alni minal-mutatahhirin;

Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdik;

Ashhadu an la ilaha illa anta;

Astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk.

When visiting the sick, say:

Allahumma rabban-nas;

Adhhib al-ba’s;

Washfi anta ash-shafi;

La shifa’a illa shifa’uk;

Shifa’an la yughadiru saqama.

For the married:

Barakallahu lak;

Wa baraka ‘alayk;

Wa jama‘a baynakuma fi khayr.

When Marry:

Allahumma inni as’aluka khayraha;

Wa khayra ma jabalta-ha ‘alayh;

Wa a‘udhu bika min sharriha;

Wa sharri ma jabalta-ha ‘alayh.

Idha ishtara ba‘iran falyakhudh bidhirwati sanamihi wa lyaqul mithla dhalik.

If one of you, when having relations with his spouse, says:

Bismillah;

Allahumma jannibna ash-shaytan;

Wa jannibi ash-shaytana ma razaqtana.

What children are protected with:

U‘idhukuma bikalimatillahi at-tammati;

Min kulli shaytanin wa hammah;

Wa min kulli ‘aynin lammah.

Duaa for someone who has loaned money when it is due:
Barakallahu laka fi ahlika wa malika;

Innama jaza’us-salafi al-hamdu wal-ada’u.

What does a Muslim say if another Muslim is praised?

Ahsibu fulanan, wallahu hasibuh;

Wa la uzakki ‘ala Allahi ahada;

Ahsibuhu — in kana ya‘lamu dhalika — kada wa kada.

What does a Muslim say when he is praised?

Allahumma la tu’akhidhni bima yaqulun;

Waghfir li ma la ya‘lamun;

Waj‘alni khayran mimma yadhunnun.

Duaa of Qunoot

Allahumma ihdini fiman hadayt;

Wa ‘afini fiman ‘afayt;

Wa tawallani fiman tawallayt;

Wa barik li fima a‘tayt;

Wa qini sharra ma qadayt;

Fa innaka taqdi wa la yuqda ‘alayk;

Innahu la yadhillu man walayt;

Wa la ya‘izzu man ‘adayt;

Tabarakta rabbana wa ta‘alayt.

Allahumma inni a‘udhu biridaka min sakhatik;

Wa bimu‘afatik min ‘uqubatik;

Wa a‘udhu bika minka;

La uhsi thana’an ‘alayk;

Anta kama athnayta ‘ala nafsik.

Allahumma iyyaka na‘bud;

Wa laka nusalli wa nasjud;

Wa ilayka nas‘a wa nahfid;

Narju rahmatak;

Wa nakhsha ‘adhabak;

Inna ‘adhabaka bil-kafirin mulhaq.

Allahumma inna nasta‘inuk;

Wa nastaghfiruk;

Wa nuthni ‘alaykal-khayr;

Wa la nakfuruk;

Wa nu’minu bik;

Wa nakhda‘u lak;

Wa nakhla‘u man yakfuruk.

Duaa to pay off debt

Allahumma malikal-mulk;

Tu’ti al-mulka man tashaa;

Wa tanzi‘ul-mulka mimman tashaa;

Wa tu‘izzu man tashaa, wa tudhillu man tashaa;

Biyadikal-khayr, innaka ‘ala kulli shay’in qadeer;

Rahmana ad-dunya wal-akhirati wa rahimahuma;

Tu‘tihima man tashaa, wa tamna‘u minhuma man tashaa;

Irhamni rahmatan tughni-ni biha ‘an rahmati man siwak.

Allahumma akfini bihalalika ‘an haramika;

Wa aghnini bifadhlika ‘amman siwak.

Allahumma inni a‘udhu bika minal-hammi wal-hazan;

Wal-‘ajzi wal-kasal;

Wal-bukhli wal-jubn;

Wa dal‘id-dayni wa ghalabatir-rijal.

Duaa against the enemy

Allahumma munzila al-kitabi, sari‘a al-hisabi, ahzimi al-ahzaba;

Allahumma ihzimhum wa zalzilhum.

Duaa for one who fears the injustice of the ruler:

Kun li jaran min Fulān ibn Fulān wa ahzābihi min khalāqika;

An yafruta ‘alayya ahadun minhum aw yatghā;

‘Azzā jaruka, wa jalla thanā’uka, wa lā ilāha illā anta.

Duaa for calamity:

Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji‘un;

Allahumma’jurni fi musibati;

Wa akhlif li khayran minha.

Duaa when closing the eyes of the dead:

Allahumma aghfir li-fulanin [name];

Warfa‘ darajatahu fil-mahdiyyin;

Wakhlufhu fi ‘aqibihi fil-ghabirin;

Waghfir lana walahu ya rabbal-‘alamin;

Wafsah lahu fi qabrih;

Wa nawwir lahu fihi.

Duaa after burying the dead:

Allahumma aghfir lahu;

Allahumma thabbit-hu.

Condolence duaa:

Inna lillahi ma akhadh;

Wa lahu ma a‘ta;

Wa kullu shay’in ‘indahu bi-ajalin musamma;

Faltasbir waltahtasib.

Visiting graves duaa:

As-salamu ‘alaykum ahlad-diyar;
Minal-mu’minina wal-muslimin;
Wa inna in sha’ Allahu bikum lahiqun;
Wa yarhamu Allahul-mustaqdimina minna wal-musta’khirin;
As’alullaha lana wa lakumul-‘afiyah.

Supplication for the dead during funeral prayers:

Allahumma aghfir lahu warhamhu;

Wa akrim nuzulahu wa wassi‘ qabrah;

Wa adkhilhu al-jannah;

Wa a‘idhhu min ‘adhabil-qabri wa ‘adhabin-nar.

Crescent sighting supplication:

Allahu akbar;

Allahumma ahillahu ‘alayna bil-amni wal-iman;

Was-salamati wal-islam;

Wat-tawfiqi lima tuhibbu rabbana wa tardha;

Rabbuna wa rabbuka Allah.

Duaa for rain:

Allahumma asqina ghaythan mughithan mari’an mari‘a;

Nafi‘an ghayra darrin, ‘ajilan ghayra ajil.

Allahumma aghithna, Allahumma aghithna, Allahumma aghithna.

Allahumma asqi ‘ibadaka wa baha’imaka;

Wanshur rahmataka, wa ahyi baladaka al-mayyit.

Wind Duaa

Allahumma inni as’aluka khayraha;

Wa a‘udhu bika min sharriha.

Allahumma inni as’aluka khayraha;

Wa khayra ma fiha;

Wa khayra ma ursilat bihi;

Wa a‘udhu bika min sharriha;

Wa sharri ma fiha;

Wa sharri ma ursilat bihi.

Thunder Duaa:

Subhana alladhi yusabbihur-ra‘du bihamdih;

Wal-mala’ikatu min khifatih.

Supplication of a fasting person if food is brought and he does not break his fast:

Idha du‘iya ahadukum falyujib;

Fa in kana sa’iman falyusalli;

Wa in kana muftiran falyat‘am.
